Z||000000||Cheever2||07-26-2001||06:17 PM||||Here's one I told about in a previous post.  It was in a grocery store parking lot.  While I was in my minivan writing a note to put on the windshield, the owner meanwhile returned and drove away.  I'll try to be more prepared (if not quicker) next time.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Yellow_Fiero20001.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Yellow_Fiero20002.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>- <I>Chuck Hodges</I> -<BR><A HREF="http://home.houston.rr.com/fieropartsrelay" TARGET=_blank> Fiero Parts Relay</A> administrator||||reg||2
Z||000001||fiero56||07-26-2001||07:15 PM||||I haven't seen that one down there before, but have seen a yellow Formula convertible running around town there before. How was vacation? I've taken a week vacation there every year for the past 9 years. Every year I go down I can see the area just exploding with more and more businesses. I wasn't able to make it down this spring, and am missing it terribly. I've been to Ed Parks twice this year, but it isn't the same as the ocean and beach farther south.||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||07-26-2001||11:48 PM||||<B><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red">NO WAY!!! MAN, WHAT A SMALL WORLD!!!!!!</B></FONT></FONT>...get this, I was in Gulf shores back in May and went to take the Dolphin Cruise. When I came out to get in my car, that very car was parked right next to me!!! Did you look inside? It had black and yellow padded seat covers. The car actually looks like crap close up lol. I even took two pics of it!! Im gonna have to take my pics to a friends house who has a scanner and post them.<BR><B><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="blue">TOO WIERD MAN!!!! WHAT ARE THE ODDS?!!!</B></FONT></FONT><P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I><p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 07-27-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000003||Cheever2||07-27-2001||08:19 AM||||That's great.  But it's a small town, with one main road going to it.  The odds are if someone who lives & works in that small town owns a Fiero, people who go there "on holiday" are fairly likely to see it.  There was a faded 84, looked high-mileage, which I think may have belonged to someone who lived & worked there also, since I saw it several times.  And I don't think it would be a car you'd take on holiday.<P>I love that phrase "on holiday".  Ever since I heard it on Chicken Run, I have been hearing it a lot.  For Cliff & Jim (Aus): we usually say "vacation" here.<BR>||||reg||1
